es/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T20:02:48-07:00","id":494284,"title":"","content":"Alright, they look nice. They have drop down tech menus? That is pretty sweet. I think the space for SI apps is a little constrictive - but nothing else seems missing. I'll try to print one out and write up an old creation on one to see how it fits. Thanks for showing the setting some love, Mr Gone - i've never been entirely satisfied with the basic TU sheets - but these look good. And thanks again Su-tehp for making that happen.<br /> <br /> Edit: Out of curiousity, what tools did you use to make these, Mr Gone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  curious 04-27-2015, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T20:28:37-07:00","id":494300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these?p=494284#post494284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, they look nice. They have drop down tech menus? That is pretty sweet. I think the space for SI apps is a little constrictive - but nothing else seems missing. I'll try to print one out and write up an old creation on one to see how it fits. Thanks for showing the setting some love, Mr Gone - i've never been entirely satisfied with the basic TU sheets - but these look good. And thanks again Su-tehp for making that happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mr. G and I have collaborated before on some game sheets. I'm sure we will again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I can't really take any credit for the original design of this sheet. As I mentioned before, it's something I found on the Internet when the Aeonverse was still being published, printed for shits and giggles and managed to keep in my Trinity books for the last 15 years. (I lost the actual PDF file years ago.) The original source of this Trinity starship sheet is long gone, I'm sure.<br /> <br /> My only misgiving about these sheets (and it's a small one) is that the Tech dropdown menu couldn't include the Greek letters Omega and Psi to denote hardtech and biotech. Mr. Gone tried, but the Adobe tool he was using just wouldn't accept the Greek letters.<br /> <br /> Whoever originally designed these sheets seemed to know what they were doing, since it looked so complete to me when I first saw it. I'm glad there's nothing missing. I just hope the Structural levels are mostly correct for each ship type. And if they're not, people can always take the freighter sheet and black out the SLs they don't need, easy peasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T20:48:55-07:00","id":494308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these?p=494300#post494300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whoever originally designed these sheets seemed to know what they were doing, since it looked so complete to me when I first saw it. I'm glad there's nothing missing. I just hope the Structural levels are mostly correct for each ship type. And if they're not, people can always take the freighter sheet and black out the SLs they don't need, easy peasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had played around with a system for ship creation based on Aberrant character creation - so being able to add/subtract health levels is one of the few things i would have liked to see - but i don't know the limits of the tool used...<br /> Regardless of that, i'm always glad for more resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T22:24:47-07:00","id":494411,"title":"","content":"Yes I included teleporters in the team. I moved the start date of all stories to post 2130. In short the Coalition was stopped prior to reaching Mars. The Proxies fell in battle against the Colony and the Thule Society emerged from the shadows to conquer most of Earth. Psions and a portion of humanity have fled to the stars the Commonwealth of Stellar Races or CSR for short is an alliance of aliens and humans (all alien races designed by me) with the established races being observers to both Earth and the CSR. I acknowledge the meta plot as established but greatly disliked many of the pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T04:33:17-07:00","id":494591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these?p=494284#post494284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, they look nice. They have drop down tech menus? That is pretty sweet. I think the space for SI apps is a little constrictive - but nothing else seems missing. I'll try to print one out and write up an old creation on one to see how it fits. Thanks for showing the setting some love, Mr Gone - i've never been entirely satisfied with the basic TU sheets - but these look good. And thanks again Su-tehp for making that happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Glad you liked how they turned out.<br /> <br /> And yea, sorry II haven't done many sheets for Trinity. I haven't played the game before, so I've only done a few things as people have asked for them. I might have a few more sheets for Aberrant since I've played that one a few times. But, maybe I'll work on more sheets when the new game comes out. Hopefully I'll get to work on the official sheets for the games...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these?p=494284#post494284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Out of curiousity, what tools did you use to make these, Mr Gone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I use a full version of Adobe Acrobat to make all my sheets. It's an older version(version 5), but it does what I need to as far as sheet work goes. It can be a pain to use sometimes, and isn't the most user friendly way to make a sheet probably, but the end result is always good. Sometimes I'll use a newer version of Acrobat to enable the forms to be saved using Reader.<br /> <br /> So yea, I use Acrobat. Though I didn't with this one(as I just used someones else sheet as a template), I always build my sheets from scratch from within Acrobat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these?p=494300#post494300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mr. G and I have collaborated before on some game sheets. I'm sure we will again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these?p=494300#post494300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only misgiving about these sheets (and it's a small one) is that the Tech dropdown menu couldn't include the Greek letters Omega and Psi to denote hardtech and biotech. Mr. Gone tried, but the Adobe tool he was using just wouldn't accept the Greek letters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, limitations of the software I guess...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these?p=494300#post494300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I just hope the Structural levels are mostly correct for each ship type. And if they're not, people can always take the freighter sheet and black out the SLs they don't need, easy peasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, True...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these?p=494308#post494308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had played around with a system for ship creation based on Aberrant character creation - so being able to add/subtract health levels is one of the few things i would have liked to see - but i don't know the limits of the tool used...<br /> Regardless of that, i'm always glad for more resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I'm not sure how to make that happen with Acrobat. While I can do check boxes, the squares are always solid black. If there were outlines, then maybe you could add or subtract via check boxes...but that won't work. It's possible it could be done with layers, but I haven't mastered that part yet. Though I did experiment with that once and did a test with a Werewolf sheet where you could change the border and artwork based on the werewolf you selected from the layers menu.<br /> <br /> Not sure that'd work well for something like this though...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T06:08:18-07:00","id":494676,"title":"","content":"Mr Gone has kindly sent his sheets over and I've uploaded them to the larger archive (follow community link in sig). They're in a subfolder titled '<span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\">Trinity - Mr Gone's Starship Sheets'.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:27:36-07:00","id":494855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/488990-trinity-starship-sheets-did-any-fan-make-these?p=494676#post494676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr Gone has kindly sent his sheets over and I've uploaded them to the larger archive (follow community link in sig). They're in a subfolder titled '<span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\">Trinity - Mr Gone's Starship Sheets'.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah cool! Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signatur